  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>%</mo></math> (w/v) solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> causes precipitation of a certain sol in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> hours. The coagulating value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> for the sol is<br />[Given : Molar mass : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
