  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The minimum concentration of an electrolyte in millimoles per litre required to cause precipitation of a sol in two hours is called coagulating value.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>means</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ml</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solution</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>contain</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>salt</mi><mo>.</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>moles</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>salt</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>58</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>72</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>moles</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>720</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>milimoles</mi></math></p><p>Since 100 ml required 720 milimoles</p><p>therefor 1 L will required 7200 milimoles.</p><p>It will coagulate in 10 hours so for 2 hours =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>14400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mili</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Note: NTA has either made mistake in question data or in options.</p>"
